---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { site, categories } from '../config/site';
---

<Base title="About" description={`What ${site.name} is, who runs it, and how to get in touch.`}>
  <div class="container section">
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>About {site.name}</h1>

      <p>
        {site.name} is a free website for school students in India and their parents. It brings together clear,
        friendly guides on five things:
      </p>
      <ul>
        {
          categories.map((c) => (
            <li>
              <a href={c.path}>{c.name}</a>: {c.blurb}
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p>
        It also has the <a href="/roadmaps/">Career Roadmaps</a> tool, which maps modern roles to the school subjects to
        keep, the Indian degrees and the entrance exams, and an <a href="/deadlines/">Upcoming Deadlines</a> page.
      </p>

      <h2>Who runs it</h2>
      <p>
        I am {site.ownerName}, a {site.ownerTitle} in Tamil Nadu, India: {site.ownerCredentials}, with more than ten
        years in education after a first career in IT consulting. I built this site and I write and check the posts.
        Every post names who wrote it, who checked the facts, and when.
      </p>
      <p>
        Counsellors answer the same questions many times over. Writing the answers down once, in one trusted place,
        means every student gets the same quality of information, and parents can read it at home. More about my work is
        on <a href={site.ownerSite}>my portfolio site</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>How to use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use the search box to look for a career, a course, a test, a university or a country.</li>
        <li>Not sure where to start? Go to <a href="/start/">Start here by grade</a>.</li>
        <li>Choosing subjects? Open the <a href="/roadmaps/">Career Roadmaps</a>.</li>
        <li>Every post has a short <strong>For Parents</strong> box near the top.</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>Save</strong> on any post to keep it in <a href="/saved/">My Saved Posts</a> on this device.</li>
        <li>Check <a href="/deadlines/">Upcoming Deadlines</a> so you never miss an application date.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Have a question, spotted a mistake, or want a topic covered? Write to me at
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}><Icon name="mail" size={18} /> {site.contactEmail}</a> or use my
        <a href={site.contactUrl}>contact page</a>. Families who would like a one to one counselling session can book one
        the same way.
      </p>

      <div class="note">
        <strong>Please note.</strong> Everything on this site is for guidance only. Fees, dates, cut-offs and rules
        change often. Always check the official link given in each post before you apply or pay for anything, and talk
        to a career counsellor before making a big decision.
      </div>

      <h2>Your privacy</h2>
      <p>
        This site does not ask you to log in and does not collect any personal information. Saved posts stay in your
        own browser and are never sent anywhere.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
